 faqIntro: 'Answers on whether SEO works for law firms, timelines, choosing a provider, ads, reviews under Law Society rules, AI search, cost and nearby towns.',
 faq: [
  ['Does SEO work for law firms?', 'Yes. Many people looking for a lawyer start on Google, in the Map Pack or with a practice-area search, so a firm that is missing there is missing from their shortlist. Law firm SEO works best when your lawyers review the pages and every page follows the Code of Conduct, because legal searches face Google\'s highest trust bar.'],
  ['How long does SEO take for law firms in Edmonton?', 'It depends on the channel. Business Profile and Map Pack improvements usually show first, because profile changes take effect quickly; practice-area pages ranking in organic results for broad terms such as "lawyer edmonton" take longer and depend on content quality and links. We give a written estimate after the audit.'],
  ['Which SEO company is best for law firms?', 'The best fit is a provider that knows the Law Society of Alberta\'s marketing rules, has your lawyers review every practice-area page and never guarantees a #1 ranking, because Google says nobody can. Ask how they handle reviews, case results and specialist claims; our guide on {{how to choose an SEO agency|blog/choosing-an-seo-agency-in-edmonton}} lists more questions.'],
  ['Should law firms run Google Ads or SEO?', 'Legal clicks are often expensive in Google Ads. Many firms use ads for specific practice areas while SEO builds, then let strong practice-area pages bring enquiries without paying per click. Compare both on cost per lead, not on clicks.'],
  ['Can a law firm ask for more Google reviews under Law Society rules?', `Yes, with care. The Code of Conduct does not list review requests among its examples of improper marketing, but its commentary flags testimonials with emotional appeals and unjustified expectations, so ask every client in the same neutral way and never suggest what to write. Google's Maps content policy also forbids rewarding reviews or asking only satisfied clients, and replies should never confirm that the reviewer was a client.`],
  ['How does AI search change law firm SEO?', 'AI answers in Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Gemini and Perplexity are built from web pages, so the practice-area pages and lawyer bios that rank are also the ones that get cited. Clear answers to common legal questions, structured data and consistent firm details help; see {{AI search optimization|services/ai-search-optimization}}.'],
  ['How much does law firm SEO cost?', 'The cost depends on how many practice areas and offices need pages and profiles, and how competitive each search is in Edmonton. Our packages and what each includes are on the {{SEO pricing|pricing}} page, and the free SEO audit shows which work matters first.'],
  ['Can a law firm rank in St. Albert and Sherwood Park without an office there?', 'Yes, through practice-area pages, but not through a Map Pack listing. Each real office can have its own Business Profile; for other towns, practice-area pages reach clients across the region in the regular results. We never create profiles for offices you do not staff.']],
 servicesIntro: '**A law firm\'s plan draws on local SEO, reviewed content and AI search optimization, because legal clients compare firms in Maps, on practice-area pages and in AI answers.**',
